(1.1 The Testing Effect in Empirical Research) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
(Numerous empirical studies demonstrate that taking a practice test produces superior retention compared to spending equal time studying the original source material. The mental effort invested in retrieving information serves as an encoding event that reorganizes cognitive schemas and identifies conceptual knowledge gaps.) Tj
0 -20 Td
(This paragraph expands upon the analytical implications for curricular design, emphasizing structured dialectical interrogation over superficial memorization.) Tj
ET

endstream
