(1.2 Socratic Cross-Examination and Cognitive Conflict) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
(The Socratic method introduces structured challenge and cognitive dissonance by presenting counterexamples and plausible misconceptions. When learners confront claims that conflict with their superficial intuition, they are compelled to articulate justifying reasons and inspect the underlying factual assumptions.) Tj
0 -20 Td
(This paragraph expands upon the analytical implications for curricular design, emphasizing structured dialectical interrogation over superficial memorization.) Tj
ET

endstream
