(1.3 Plausible Distractors and Discrimination Learning) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
(Designing high-quality assessment items requires crafting plausible distractors that reflect common cognitive biases and semantic confusions rather than trivial falsehoods. Evaluating whether a subtle variation represents truth or distortion engages higher-order critical evaluation.) Tj
0 -20 Td
(This paragraph expands upon the analytical implications for curricular design, emphasizing structured dialectical interrogation over superficial memorization.) Tj
ET

