(1.4 Retrieval Practice Under Epistemic Uncertainty) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
(When individuals encounter questions with subtle lies, their confidence calibration is rigorously tested. High confidence combined with incorrect assertions indicates overconfidence or illusion of competence, which can only be mitigated through immediate, verifiable source evidence.) Tj
0 -20 Td
(This paragraph expands upon the analytical implications for curricular design, emphasizing structured dialectical interrogation over superficial memorization.) Tj
ET

