(1.8 Distributed Practice and Desirable Difficulties) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
(Introducing desirable difficulties, such as spaced intervals and interleaved topics, creates short-term friction that yields long-term fluency. Retrieval practice functions as a cornerstone of distributed learning systems by maintaining accessible memory paths.) Tj
0 -20 Td
(This paragraph expands upon the analytical implications for curricular design, emphasizing structured dialectical interrogation over superficial memorization.) Tj
